  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Big River** (1 review): The stretch from Big River through U.S. Blues stood out to this attendee as outstanding [3]\n- **Shakedown Street** (1 review): Listener liked how the band worked the rhythm during Shakedown Street [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Big River**: back after 43 archived shows (807 days) [5]\n- **Johnny B. Goode**: back after 74 archived shows (1160 days); rare: 13 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2021-09-13.HollywoodCasinoAmpitheatreMO** (recommended): audience recording; 19 songs; 180 min; rated 3.33/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer finds it has a front-of-board-like quality, yet with fairly noticeable but not intrusive crowd chatter, and sounds great [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended the show in person and enjoyed it equally live and on the recording [3]\n- Reviewer usually prefers recordings made from over-the-shoulder positions at this venue, but still likes this one [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2021-09-13.HollywoodCasinoAmpitheatreMO**: taped by W Zimmerman; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Sennheiser ME80's > GakCables > MixPre 6 @ 16/48 [1]. Also: Audience recording: Sennheiser ME80 mics, GakCables, MixPre 6 recorder at 16-bit/48k, edited in Sound Forge Pro 13, converted to FLAC with Traders Little Helper [1]",
